---
import Button from "./Button.astro";
import { skillDownloadPath, skillVersion } from "../lib/skillDownload";
// Styles are inline so they ship only on the guide that shows the download, leaving the
// shared guide stylesheet (and every other guide page) unchanged.
---

<aside class="skill card" aria-labelledby="guide-skill-title">
  <p class="skill__tag">Manual download · Claude skill</p>
  <h2 class="skill__title" id="guide-skill-title">Run this check in Claude</h2>
  <p>
    The ScholarMark Citation Audit skill gives Claude the checks in this guide. Paste your draft
    and the source passages you have, and it reports a status, a confidence level and a next step
    for each claim, quotation, page number and DOI, along with what it couldn't check.
  </p>

  <ol class="skill__steps">
    <li>Download the ZIP. Keep it zipped.</li>
    <li>
      In Claude, open <strong>Customize → Skills</strong>, choose <strong>Add</strong>, then
      <strong>Upload skill</strong>, and pick the file. Some accounts show this under
      <strong>Plugins</strong>. Skills need code execution turned on in Settings → Capabilities.
    </li>
    <li>In Claude Code, unzip it into <code>~/.claude/skills/</code> instead.</li>
  </ol>

  <p class="skill__prompt-label">Then try:</p>
  <p class="skill__prompt">
    “Audit the citations in this paragraph against the source excerpts I’ve pasted below. Flag
    quotes that don’t match word for word and page numbers you can’t confirm.”
  </p>

  <p class="skill__fine">
    The skill works on text in the chat. It needs no account and stores nothing. Searching your
    saved ScholarMark library uses the separate ScholarMark connector. Features vary by Claude plan
    and app; DOI lookups need web access. This is a manual download, not an app directory listing.
  </p>

  <Button href={skillDownloadPath} variant="secondary" download>
    Download the skill (ZIP, v{skillVersion})
  </Button>
</aside>

<style is:inline>
  .skill {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.975rem;
  }

  .skill p,
  .skill li {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .skill__tag {
    justify-self: start;
    padding: 0.05rem 0.5rem;
    border: 1px dashed var(--muted);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .skill .skill__title {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .skill__steps {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .skill__steps code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .skill .skill__prompt-label {
    margin-bottom: -0.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .skill .skill__prompt {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0;
    background: var(--paper-deep);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
  }

  .skill .skill__fine {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .skill .btn {
    justify-self: start;
  }
</style>
